Hi experts

Last week I asked if there is any possibility to synchronize the time
of our OSF/1 machines to the clock of our VMS cluster.

The solution seems to be that we set up our VMS cluster as a ntp server. NTP is a TCP/IP time synchronization protocol which is included in several 
different third party TCP/IP products for VMS. 

I knew that ntp can be used in UNIX environments, but had no idea that NTP also
can be used on a VAX. So I will try to implement this ntp/xntp (well me -> 
our VMS crack).

Another proposal was, that we could sync with Internet NTP or put a DCF77
in a Linux and serve ntp from there.

