To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Re: remote printing to my alpha
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075319106591

Hi,

I assume you have the problem of a CTRL-D character at the beginning
of the printfile created by windows.
It confuses the printfilter of the UNIX.

If this is the case,
you should insert the following line in your win.ini file in the PC:

[printer name,lpt1]     <------- something like this should already be in your file
ctrld=0		        <------- this line should be added.

hope  this helps.

