>> I did not check the SCSI ID for the slot which happened to be 4. After
>> booting up, the system could see the RZ28 disk as ID=4. Comming to use the
>> QIC-150 tape, a week later it did'nt work - setting the SCSI-ID to 5 or 6 it 
>> fails to work anymore ( the system does not pick it up using 'show device' ).
>>
>> Could this of damaged the QIC-150 controller somehow ?
>> 
>> At the time this happened I also had a TLZ07 dat tape set to SCSI-ID=5, it
>> was not affected and continues to work fine.
>> 
>> Any help or suggestions are greatly appreciated.

Most responces suggested to check the /dev files and perform a doconfig. None
of this worked as the SCSI-ID of the QIC-150 tape unit was permantly set to
ID=4, the RZ28 hard disk continued to use ID=4, as the tape unit was last on
the scsi chain it was never seen by 'show device'.

The problem was that the SCSI-ID connector switch was connected to the
controller board the wrong way round, so what ever setting you chose it still
used ID=4. Fixing this all was well.

It was just my luck all things worked fine when I first installed the tape
unit and chose the SCSI-ID=4.

Thanks to all who responded..

Joe
