From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Apr 06 21:08:18 1995
From: holtzman () mit ! edu
Date: Thu, 06 Apr 1995 21:08:18 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: How do I config vmunix for SCSI Id's 8-15 on KZTSA?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075319106402


The answer, from two sources within Digital (Dr. Blinn & Alan Rollow),
is that Digital Unix (TM) does not yet support wide mode SCSI addressing,
so you can't get to the upper 8 device addresses (8-15).

I did determine, on my own, that you can get a full 8 devices (rather
than 7) by setting the KZTSA to use a SCSI ID of 8 or above.  This leaves
all the Digital Unix (TM) recognized addresses free for peripherals.

-Henry

